  "order": 143,
  "url": "/js/js_htmldom_html.asp",
  "title": "HTML DOM - Changing HTML",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "HTML DOM - Changing HTML"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Changing HTML Content"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The HTML DOM allows JavaScript to change both the text and the content of HTML elements."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The easiest way to modify the content is by using the innerHTML property:"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "document.getElementById(id).innerHTML = new HTML"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "The innerHTML Property"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The easiest way to get the content of an element is by using the innerHTML property."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The innerHTML property is useful for getting or replacing the content of HTML elements."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The innerHTML property can be used to get or change any HTML element,\nincluding <html> and <body>."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Common Mistakes"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "Trying to access a DOM element before it exists",
        "Forgetting the quotes in an id like \"demo\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "html",
      "text": "<html>\n\n<body>\n\n<p id=\"p1\">Hello World!</p>\n\n<script>\n\ndocument.getElementById(\"p1\").innerHTML = \"New text!\";\n\n</script>\n\n</body>\n\n</html>",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_change_innerhtml"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Example explained:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "The HTML document above contains a <p> element with id=\"p1\"",
        "We use the HTML DOM to get the element with id=\"p1\"",
        "A JavaScript changes the content (innerHTML) of that element to \"New\n  text!\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "html",
      "text": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n\n<body>\n\n<h1 id=\"id01\">Old Heading</h1>\n\n<script>\n\nconst element = document.getElementById(\"id01\");\nelement.innerHTML = \"New Heading\";\n\n</script>\n\n</body>\n\n</html>",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_dom_innerhtml"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Example explained:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "The HTML document above contains an <h1> element with id=\"id01\"",
        "We use the HTML DOM to get the element with id=\"id01\"",
        "A JavaScript changes the content (innerHTML) of that element to \"New\n  Heading\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Changing an Attribute"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "To change the value of an HTML attribute, use this syntax:"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "document.getElementById(id).attribute = new value"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "html",
      "text": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n\n<body>\n\n<img id=\"myImage\" src=\"smiley.gif\">\n\n<script>\n\ndocument.getElementById(\"myImage\").src = \"landscape.jpg\";\n\n</script>\n\n</body>\n\n</html>",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_dom_image"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Example explained:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "The HTML document above contains an <img> element with id=\"myImage\"",
        "We use the HTML DOM to get the element with id=\"myImage\"",
        "A JavaScript changes the src attribute of that element from \"smiley.gif\" to \"landscape.jpg\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Dynamic HTML content"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "JavaScript can create dynamic HTML content:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "html",
      "text": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n\n<body>\n\n<script>\n\ndocument.getElementById(\"demo\").innerHTML = \"Date : \" + Date();\n\n</script>\n\n</body>\n\n</html>",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_dom_date"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "document.write()"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "In JavaScript, document.write() can be used to write directly to the HTML\noutput stream:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "html",
      "text": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n\n<body>\n\n<p>Bla bla bla</p>\n\n<script>\n\ndocument.write(Date());\n\n</script>\n\n<p>Bla bla bla</p>\n\n</body>\n\n</html>",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_dom_write"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Warning !"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Never use document.write() after the document is loaded. It will\noverwrite the document."
    }
  ]
}
